 ### Tandem Algorithm with Dumping
-A strategy that enhances the tandem algorithm by reducing the number of generated triangles through a dumping mechanism, specifically handling disconnected components to allow interactive exploration [S3]. It filters small components based on geometric criteria (volume) [S3]. On a 1626x7028x2000 dataset, it extracted surfaces in 5 minutes using 56 processors, compared to more than 3 hours for the sequential version [S3]. It reduces disconnected components from 18,111 to 328 [S3]. This is applied to seismic cubes for hydrocarbon exploration [S3].
